<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 268)</h2>
<p><b>Web Review: the player-completeness release.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>The web page gains frame ticks, an in/out loop range (mirrored with the app both directions), loop/ping-pong/play-once, speed control, <b>audio with volume and mute</b>, a waveform strip, and the app's keyboard shortcuts — Space, J/K/L, I/O, [ ], M, W, B/A/R.</li>
<li><b>Comment parity</b>: global session notes, text annotations and "N marks" rows now appear in the web notes list, composer on top — same reading order as the app.</li>
<li>Web markup lands on the exact frame the app is looking at — the one-frame drift at 23.976 is gone (frame rates are carried as rational values now), and drawing no longer smears while the pen is down.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
